 "title": "Auditor's Office - Welcome to Day County, South Dakota!",
 "text": "Auditor's Office - Welcome to Day County, South Dakota!\nOctober 18, 2026\nWelcome to Day County, South Dakota!\nHome\nDirectory »\nAmbulance\nAuditor’s Office\nClerk of Courts\nCommunity Health Nurse / WIC Office\nDirector of Equalization (Assessor’s Office)\nDriver’s License\nEmergency Management Office\nExtension Office\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning Office\nRegister of Deeds’ Office\nSheriff’s Office\nState’s Attorney\nTreasurer’s Office\nVeterans Service Office\nWeed & Pest\nWelfare Office\nCommission »\nCommission Agenda\nCommission Minutes\nElections\nEmployment\nCities/Towns\nTownship\nAlerts\nCounty GIS\nYou are here: Home / Auditor’s Office\nAuditor’s Office\nHOURS: 8:00am – 5:00pm Monday-Friday\nTonya Lehman, Day County Auditor\n711 W. 1 st Street, Suite 204\nWebster, SD 57274\n(605) 345-9500\nAuditor@day.sdcounty.gov\nSarah Bremmon, Deputy Auditor\nNicole Kwasniewski, Deputy Auditor/Welfare Director\nKarli Zimmerman, Part-time Deputy Auditor\nThe Auditor is the county business manager. The Auditor is responsible for commissioners’ proceedings, agendas and records, accounting records, revenue and expense reports, voter registration and elections. Businesses located outside of city limits apply for beer and liquor licenses with the Auditor. The Auditor also figures real estate and mobile home taxes and handles county bid lettings. In many cases, the Auditor also manages medical indigent claims.\nElections\nStatewide Ballot Measures 2026\nAbsentee Request Form\nVoter Information Portal (V.I.P.)\nVoter Registration Form\nDay County Precinct List\nAuditor\nAbatement Form\nAudit 2024 / 2023\nMill Levies 2025\n(2025 taxes are payable in 2026)\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in",
